This workflow extracts and generalizes the Cancer Communications glioma RNA
revision analysis scripts supplied by the author. Original analytical
definitions, source provenance, and deliberate refactoring changes are
documented in README.md and docs/.

DRIMSeq numerical adapter
The DTU engine adapts private R helpers from DRIMSeq 1.38.0, by Malgorzata
Nowicka and the DRIMSeq contributors. DRIMSeq is distributed under GNU GPL
version 3 or later. The adapted helpers remain under that compatible license.
They are not an unmodified DRIMSeq release and are not represented as an
upstream-approved patch. Preserve this notice, upstream attribution and the
version guard when redistributing the adapted code.

DRIMSeq project: https://bioconductor.org/packages/DRIMSeq/
Upstream source: https://git.bioconductor.org/packages/DRIMSeq
Citation: Nowicka M, Robinson MD. DRIMSeq: a Dirichlet-multinomial framework for
multivariate count outcomes in genomics. F1000Research. 2016;5:1356.
doi:10.12688/f1000research.8900.2

Other dependencies are separate projects under their respective licenses.
Use citation("DRIMSeq"), citation("stageR"), citation("vegan") and citation()
for the installed software's current bibliographic records. Reference genome,
gene annotation and pathway data retain their original terms and citations.

No raw patient sequence data or reference databases are bundled here. The
metadata file records original local input paths; users control access to
those files. No external repository was created or published by this task.

